            <ArticleTitle>Substituted coumarins as potent 5-lipoxygenase inhibitors.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2528-31</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Leukotriene biosynthesis inhibitors have potential as therapeutic agents for asthma and inflammatory diseases. A novel series of substituted coumarin derivatives has been synthesized and the structure-activity relationship was evaluated with respect to their ability to inhibit the formation of leukotrienes via the human 5-lipoxygenase enzyme.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
